WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.050
- [Interviewer] All right. Pepper.

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:05.883
- Yes, sir.

00:00:05.883 --> 00:00:06.820
- [Interviewer] Pepper,
oh, where'd you grow up?

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:07.860
Where are you from originally?

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.100
- [Pepper] I'm from Iowa.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.263
I'm born and raised in
Ames, Iowa, Boone County.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:13.943
- [Interviewer] So tell
me about your family.

00:00:13.943 --> 00:00:16.400
You had both of your
parents when you were a kid?

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.610
- [Pepper] I know of my mother real well.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.060
Cause I'm like her.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.010
My mother is straight up hippie.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.630
My mother married a Klan member.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.503
My dad's the head of one
of the Klans out there.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.060
So at the age 12, he guy,
he was racing stock cars.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:34.930
Got in an accident.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.600
Flipped off in the grass.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.543
Killed two kids and got
himself in a body cast.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.090
My dad come to me and he's like, son,

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.500
you have to hold Klan meeting tonight.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.803
You're my only boy. You got nine sisters.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.410
How quickly I inventoried myself.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.563
I'm like, I'm not part of this.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.840
I'm a flower child.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.993
1966, July 9th.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.813
I do not believe in your
Klan ways or Klan shit.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.830
Don't force it on me.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.060
It's not of my realm.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.300
I'm a flower child.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.070
Peace and love and pop some pills.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:11.903
Get high.

00:01:11.903 --> 00:01:12.736
Let's make love.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.720
My dad got angry and
said, "You're not my son."

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.320
I said, "You're not my dad."

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.130
My dad wouldn't be a
coward behind the sheep,

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.740
Burning it, burning a live animal was

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.470
representing people.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:29.400
My dad would not be hateful
towards the everyone.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.840
So you see, I come from a family

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.573
that's really torn apart by hatred.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.673
At the age 14, I left.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:42.817
I told my mother, "Mom, I
need to get up out this shit."

00:01:43.938 --> 00:01:46.081
I mean, he just smashed it.

00:01:46.081 --> 00:01:47.655
Same table eating.

00:01:47.655 --> 00:01:49.130
I'm sitting with a
butcher knife in my hand

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.720
with a fork saying "God, I
wish you'd say something to me.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.237
So sick of your shit."

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.703
So at the age of 14, I got my first car.

00:01:58.703 --> 00:02:01.470
I was working at Hormel slaughter house.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:05.870
The youngest worker there,
but my friend owned it

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.920
and I told him, I need to leave soon.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.063
I can't live in this house
with this hatred, this guy.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.640
So when I hit 14, I got my Nova

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.197
and I really didn't want
to leave my mom behind.

00:02:24.197 --> 00:02:25.730
"Like mom, get in the car.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:26.787
Let's go."

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.040
She's like "I can't.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.410
He'll come looking like last
time and beat me again."

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.748
Like "Mom, how many, how many beatings,

00:02:34.748 --> 00:02:36.690
beatings you gotta take
every week for nothing?

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.170
When he gets drunk he just beats on you."

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:42.133
I take every week for nothing.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:46.033
So you see, I was forced to
inventory myself at a young age.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.930
What do I really want in life?

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.590
What am I?

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:52.453
Who am I?

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.890
Am I? And you know what?

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:00.320
All my life I've been
searching for one thing.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.223
And I know I'll never find it.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.410
A father and son relationship
like the rest of the people.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.113
Something I, I don't have.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.280
I mean, I can have all
the money in the world

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.080
but can I buy true love
from a dad or something?

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:18.943
No, you can't.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.674
So you'll see, I pack up my bags.

00:03:22.674 --> 00:03:24.843
I'd saved up like $2,300.

00:03:27.135 --> 00:03:29.963
I'd been stocking on Chevron gas cards.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.410
I knew I had to leave home.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.110
I couldn't deal with this no more.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.110
My mother begged, "Let me
give you all my life savings.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.210
Make sure you're safe. When
you gonna come back home?"

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:46.160
I'm like, "I'm not. I'm not.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.400
As long as he's alive.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.900
I'm not. I'm not part of this.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.130
You cannot force that.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.550
It's a shoe that don't fit.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.813
Don't so understand?

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.730
I'm a flower child.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.820
I'm a off-breed of the hippies.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.695
The next generation, the hippies is us.

00:04:02.695 --> 00:04:05.747
I need to live my life
and make something of me."

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:12.100
I swore to myself from, from a young age

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.813
I'd never be like my dad.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.721
Well I don't know how my
dad had it happen or what.

00:04:19.721 --> 00:04:21.080
I don't know the issues. Nothing.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.440
I know he had some gunplay.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.653
He got half a finger. It's
a stubby, but it's half.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.207
Well, when I was working at Hormel,

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.040
I had an accident.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.530
One of the saw bands broke and flew up

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.523
and I had time to go like this.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.623
I amputated tip of my fingers.

00:04:48.464 --> 00:04:53.464
I'm like, "Damn it! Mom,
look. I'm like my dad.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.680
I told you I didn't want to stay here."

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:59.640
She's like "No, baby. You
lost the tip of your finger.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.140
Your dad has half a nub."

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:05.050
Like "Mom, it's an omen. I gotta go.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.410
I gotta go."

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.660
That was part of it.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.873
My hand started looking
like my dad's hand.

00:05:14.349 --> 00:05:15.813
And my mother swore up and down

00:05:15.813 --> 00:05:17.630
"Baby, you still damn
near your whole finger.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.560
Just the tip of your finger was cut off."

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.250
I'm like "Mom, it's still
a stubby. Still a stubby."

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.210
She's like "No, your dad
ain't got no finger now.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.810
You got a messed up part of a finger now,

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.150
but you got a finger now.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.247
It's not a stubby."

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:34.303
Mom did everything she could.

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:38.230
I just say, mom tried to
give me all her life savings.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:42.560
I told her "No. I'm man.
I got 21 Chevron cards

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.153
with $160 worth of gas on it.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.393
I got like 14,000 in my pocket.

00:05:51.105 --> 00:05:52.937
I can't do this no more."

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.753
My mom passed me a backpack.

00:06:01.886 --> 00:06:03.980
And I called her a week on the road.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:08.630
